                %sup#fnref:1
                  %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the mid 1970s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julian+Cole"} Julian Cole
            proposed a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos-theoretic
            construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+%28geometry%29"} spectra in geometry
            arising in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+commutative+ring"} spectrum of a commutative ring
            but for more general
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theories"} (algebraic) theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoints"} right adjoints
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functors"} forgetful functors
            that generalized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Monique+Hakim"} M. Hakim's
            approach to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+topos"} locally ringed toposes
          %p
            Basic ingredients are pairs of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theories"} geometric theories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            over the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/language"} language
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            results from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            by addition of further
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}-Mod_\mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}-Mod_\mathcal{E}
            and the spectrum construction can be viewed as a sort of generalization of a right adjoint to the inclusion. The quotient relation between the two theories gives the construction a model-theoretic flavor.
          %h3#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                  %mo −
                  %mi 𝔗𝔬𝔭
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}-\mathfrak{Top}
            of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-modelled+toposes"} T-modelled toposes
            is given as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                objects are pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},M)
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                is a topos and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                a
                = succeed "-model" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕋
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℰ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %li
              %p
                1-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{F},L)\to (\mathcal{E},M)
                are pairs
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,f)
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℱ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{E}
                a geometric morphism and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:p^*M\to L
                a
                = succeed "-model" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝕋
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            %li
              %p
                2-cells
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi q
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,f)\to(q,g)
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo :
                      %mi p
                      %mo →
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta:p\to q
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi M
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f=g\circ\eta_M
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔗𝔬𝔭
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}-\mathfrak{Top}_N
            is the full sub-2-category on pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E},M)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
          %h3#definition_2 Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            be a (geometric) quotient theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
            of
            = succeed "-model" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            %em admissible
            if
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
